  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2007-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The equations become \\(3^a = 3^{4(b+2)}\\) and \\(5^{3b} = 5^{a-3}.\\)\n\nSo \\(a = 4(b + 2)\\) and \\(3b = a - 3.\\)\n\nSolving gives \\(a = -12\\) and \\(b = -5,\\) so \\(ab = 60.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite \\(81 = 3^4\\) and \\(125 = 5^3\\) to match the bases",
        "Equating exponents gives \\(a = 4(b + 2)\\) and \\(3b = a - 3\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
